From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:48:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(allwinner): use 1KB per-core stack size

The previous definition (0x1000 / PLATFORM_CORE_COUNT) allocated 1 KB
per core on existing 4-core SoCs. However, upcoming SoCs like the A523
and A733 have 8 cores, which would reduce the per-core stack to 512 bytes.
This is dangerously tight for multi-core exception handling and PSCI
power management routines.

Define PLATFORM_STACK_SIZE directly as 0x400 (1 KB) per core. This is a
NOP for existing 4-core platforms, while ensuring upcoming SoCs with
higher core counts have adequate stack headroom.

Signed-off-by: Alastair D'Silva <alastair@d-silva.org>
Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/55202
---
 plat/allwinner/common/include/platform_def.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/include/platform_def.h b/plat/allwinner/common/include/platform_def.h
index 1131dd66a..59ccafb96 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/include/platform_def.h
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/include/platform_def.h
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 #define PLATFORM_CLUSTER_COUNT		U(1)
 #define PLATFORM_CORE_COUNT		(PLATFORM_CLUSTER_COUNT * \
 					 PLATFORM_MAX_CPUS_PER_CLUSTER)
-#define PLATFORM_STACK_SIZE		(0x1000 / PLATFORM_CORE_COUNT)
+#define PLATFORM_STACK_SIZE		0x400
 
 #ifndef SPD_none
 #ifndef BL32_BASE
